# Offline AI and voice
- Use explicitly selected on-device models only; no external inference APIs, hosted fallback, provider keys, or Goblin Tools integration/assets/branding. Verify current implementation and `docs/OFFLINE_VOICE.md`.
- Reuse `VoiceCapture`, `VoiceTaskParser`, and `VoiceTaskService` after confirming their APIs. Keep AI behind typed contracts; don't add per-feature backends or agents.
- Treat model output as a draft: user action is required to apply it. Never auto-complete tasks, award rewards, send replies, or execute generated code.
- Use selected context only and retain no AI history by default. Keep AI estimates separate from measured time/rewards; validate estimates and preserve Hive/legacy step contracts.
- Test malformed/empty output, timeout, stale/duplicate apply, and timer restart/background cases when affected. Optional legacy sync stays separate and disabled by default.
